    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 16 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: As declarer, score at least 36 card points (35⅔ rounded up) from tricks and talon to win the contract; defenders win if declarer fails. Optional announcements (win last trick with Trump I, or Valat) add bonus risk and reward.',
      'Turn-flow example: Bidding: Forehand opens; players pass or bid Dreier, Unterer, Oberer, or Solo in ascending order; overcall or hold. Highest bidder is declarer. In Dreier/Unterer/Oberer the declarer exposes both talon halves, picks one, discards three cards (no Kings or Trull; tarocks only if no option, then shown to defenders); unused half counts to defenders. In Solo, talon is set aside for defenders. Announcements: win last trick with Trump I, or Valat (win every trick). Play: Anticlockwise from forehand. Must follow suit if able; otherwise must play a trump; otherwise may discard. Scoring: Tarock packet scheme; declarer needs 36+ points to win.',
      'Scoring example: Card points in packets of three, 2 deducted per packet; declarer needs 36 (35⅔ rounded up) to win. Game values: Dreier 3, Unterer 4, Oberer 5, Solo 8, Valat 12 or 24 announced. Bonuses for Köpfe, Tarock Trull, Royal Trull, Pagat Ultimo, Valat. Declarer wins by taking 36+ card points; defenders win if declarer fails. Optional announcements add bonus points..',
